  "final_message": "The blog is built: a Flask API under `/api` with all the endpoints you listed, plus a React frontend that the backend serves. The Docker image build wasn't run, because Docker isn't available in this sandbox.\n\nWhat I did run:\n- **API:** I ran the main API flows through Flask's test client, covering register, login, publish, validation errors, edit, the 403 for editing another author's post, take-down and delete.\n- **Server:** I started the app under gunicorn. `/api/health` answered `{\"status\": \"ok\"}`, `/posts/1` returned the frontend page, and an unknown `/api/...` path returned 404.\n- **Frontend:** `npm run build` (which runs `tsc` first, then `vite build`) completes. I never opened the frontend in a browser.\n\nThings you might not expect:\n- **Usernames:** they are case-insensitive, so registering `Bob` after `bob` returns 409.\n- **Register validation:** a username must be 3\u201332 characters from letters, digits, `_`, `.` and `-`. A password must be 8\u2013128 characters.\n- **Tags:** at most 10 per post, 30 characters each, and duplicates are dropped ignoring case.\n- **Admin sign-in:** `admin` can only sign in when `ADMIN_PASSWORD` is set and non-empty, and `register` rejects that name.\n- **Sessions:** tokens last 7 days.\n- **Extras beyond the spec:** `GET /api/auth/me` tells the frontend who is signed in. Admins also get a `taken_down` flag on posts and a \"Show taken-down posts\" filter, so they can restore a post.\n- **Admin role:** the admin sees the take-down button on every post, but cannot edit or delete other people's posts.\n\nI added Tailwind, `react-router-dom` and TypeScript to the frontend and updated `package-lock.json`. I also added a `.gitignore`. The backend dependencies are unchanged, so `requirements.lock` is as it was.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
